## v0.30.0

### v0.30.0 — post-v0.29 window (10 Nov → 26 Nov 2026)

Consolidated notes for the ~1,600-commit window between the v0.29.0
draft cutoff and the v0.30.0 tag. This is a themes pass, not an
exhaustive per-commit sweep — the window was dominated by the
repository split, the money-plane correctness cluster, and the
large refactor waves. Topic logs carry the per-subsystem detail.

### Repository split and public export (#2956 epic, #2969)

- **Operations corpus carved out of the product repo** (#2964/#2965):
  all `ops/`/`scripts/ops` deployment, monitoring, and fleet tooling
  moved to the private `aitbc-ops` repository; the product checkout is
  ~71k lines lighter. Fleet relinked — OPS paths resolve through
  `/opt/aitbc-ops` on every host, zero new unit failures.
- **AGPLv3 relicensing** of the product core (#2972-era): license
  headers and `LICENSE` updated; commercial-licensing contact line
  restored. **Trademark carve-out**: AITBC marks are excluded from the
  copyright grant (`95c1942ffa`).
- **Public GitHub mirror rebuilt by history rewrite** (#2969):
  `git filter-repo` pipeline in `aitbc-ops`
  (`scripts/ops/export-public-github.py`) excises ops paths, scrubs
  host topology from blobs/commit messages/identity headers, and
  preserves golden chain fixtures. The old GitHub repo was deleted and
  recreated empty (zero stars/forks/watchers; the only true purge for
  GitHub-retained `refs/pull/*` objects). Fresh-clone verifier: all
  ten gates green — fsck clean, zero forbidden paths, zero topology
  hits, HEAD tree byte-identical, 47 tags, deterministic double-run.
  Gitea remains canonical; the mirror is export-only.
- **Release docs reorganized** topic-first (#2974): per-version log
  directories folded into `2026/<topic>_release.log` files with a
  `versions/` archive and `MANIFEST.csv`.

### Money-plane correctness cluster (Nov 23–25)

A coordinated audit-and-fix wave across escrow, market settlement,
wallet release paths, and coordinator reconciliation:

- **Escrow/settlement**: settle-CAS arbitration and on-chain outcome
  reconciliation on lost CAS (#2855); partial unique indexes on
  `client_ref`/`bids.tx_hash` so one payment settles one bid (#2858,
  #2848); sealed-verdict adoption on hashless settle; escrow residue
  leg matching by exact payload `job_id`; coordinator escrow state
  reconciled with chain truth on lock rejection; refund relay dedup
  and client_id resolution hardened.
- **Wallet release proofs**: release nonces proven free on `pending`
  (not just `latest`); reverted release receipts gated on confirmation
  depth; `released_at` stamped only on release intent; sell/exchange
  ETH release gated on admissible fresh status and non-positive
  amounts rejected.
- **Market audit cluster**: registry row repair on identical-offer
  skip; offer floor escrow sizing with unsealed-refund retry; signed
  provider pin confirmations; `MAX_PAYMENT_AMOUNT` aligned to
  `Numeric(20,8)`; service price/price_unit validation; pin-confirm
  size/hash bounds; dispute adjudication reroute of settled escrow.
- **Agent-coordinator**: escrow replay terms cover timeout/reinvest;
  refund on post-lock distribution failure; rejected release/refund
  txs reconciled to LOCKED.

### IPFS market hosting propagation (#2967, #2968)

- **Signed CAR fallback rescue**: provider pinning sweeps that cannot
  reach buyer↔provider bitswap fetch a CAR over the hub coordinator
  and verify every block against its CID multihash before it enters
  the blockstore — transport is never authority; weak hashes fail
  closed.
- Rental release gated on provider delivery attestation; escrow locks
  sized at the offer floor; miner execution keeps market IPFS escrow
  rails out of the job path; `aitbc market ipfs attest` CLI surface.
- Refund direction is fail-closed: a provider failure report can only
  refund the buyer, never pay the provider — the 30-day money-lock
  failure mode is closed.

### Bond slash lifecycle (#2966, #2976)

- Bond suspension and appeal separated from on-chain slashing
  (`d160a62e93`).
- **Pre-burn appeal window** for automatic bond slashing (`b9853f682d`):
  slash intents enter a challenge window before the burn executes.

### ZK unsafe-model unpaid execution (#2951)

- Coordinator refuses 422 before any escrow when the ZK rule fires and
  the resolved model has no `MODEL_CIRCUITS` entry; dispatch backstop
  skips such jobs for internal callers; CLI `aitbc ai submit --wait`
  handles the pending-acceptance/retry interlock correctly.

### Cross-cutting

- **Refactor waves** (#1860, #1867, c901 ratchet): 1–2k-line band
  modules split across coordinator-api, market, sync, exchange, RPC,
  MCP, and wallet; broad exception handlers narrowed; dead services
  and dead model tables removed.
- **Mempool**: unsigned protocol writes drain behind the sender's
  signed run (`bf88229636`).
- **Ops-signer**: identical payments deduped; ambiguous sends reported.

