### PG-TARGET-1 (stream 2) — schema baselines, drift and downgrades (#436)

- coordinator: ``add_global_marketplace`` seeded ``marketplace_regions``
  with ``'active'`` while 001's ``regionstatus`` enum carries the member
  names ``'ACTIVE'…'DEPRECATED'`` — valid on SQLite, fatal on PostgreSQL
  and invisible to the model either way. The seed now writes ``'ACTIVE'``
  and new revision ``f7e8d9c0b1a2`` heals databases that already carry
  lowercase rows.
- gpu: ``4d6e9c8a1b52`` probed columns with SQLite-only
  ``PRAGMA table_info``; it now uses ``sa.inspect`` (and drops its own
  index before the batch column drop). New baseline revision
  ``0001a2b3c4d5`` makes ``upgrade head`` on an empty database create
  every ``gpu_metadata`` table — the chain was previously
  alteration-only and left ``create_all`` untracked.
- edge: same baseline gap; new revision ``0001b2c3d4e5`` creates all
  ``SQLModel.metadata`` tables and ``e1c47b09f2a6`` is re-parented onto
