- pool-hub: ``c3b2d6e7f8a9``'s downgrade dropped indexes owned by
  ``b2a1c4d5e6f7`` and ``a58c1f3b3e87``, breaking the chain's downgrade;
  it now drops exactly the three indexes it creates (``if_exists``).
  ``d4c3e7f8a9b0`` used bare ``alter_column(nullable=…)`` — a ``SET NOT
  NULL`` SQLite cannot run — and now uses batch mode on SQLite (native
  ALTER on PostgreSQL) with separately-created indexes restored after
  the rebuild.
- trading: ``002``'s downgrade altered ``trade_agreements``,
  ``trade_settlements`` and ``trading_analytics``, all created by
  ``003`` and therefore already dropped at that point; the downgrade now
  mirrors the upgrade's inspector guards.
- governance: 001 declared every Decimal model column ``sa.Float()``
  (``DOUBLE PRECISION`` on PostgreSQL). New revision ``004`` converts
  them to ``Numeric(20, 8)``; ``proposals.passing_threshold`` stays
  Float — the model keeps it a ratio.
- Offline tests per app run ``upgrade head`` / ``downgrade base`` on a
