### MSG-8

- docs/design/msg8-direct-messages.md — Phase 0 design for encrypted
  direct messages: separate published X25519 key bound by a signed
  dm_key envelope, libsodium crypto_box with ephemeral sender keys,
  ciphertext-only index, client-side decryption, ~3900 B plaintext cap
  under the 4 KiB body cap. No forward secrecy; Phase 1 requires
  operator authorization plus independent crypto review.

### MSG-8b

- docs/design/msg8-direct-messages.md amended for review: SealedBox
  (library-derived nonce, no nonce field), mandatory authenticated
  inner header (closes ciphertext rebinding), crypto fields as
  top-level envelope keys (ct <= 4096 b64, plaintext ~2920 B), dm
  slug reserved in listings/totals/moderation, sender-copy = local
  plaintext (a), no dm_key chaining (wallet stays sole root).


### MSG-6

- Messaging index operability: `aitbc_messaging_*` metrics (index height, lag vs chain head, message/action totals, reads, read errors, admission rejects by coarse reason) refreshed at `/metrics` scrape time; checkpoint index digest — SHA-256 over valid envelopes at the last full 1000-block checkpoint, cached per (chain, checkpoint, head hash), computed lazily at read/scrape only (no block-import hook, no consensus change) — exported as `aitbc_messaging_index_digest{chain_id,checkpoint,digest}` for cross-node divergence checks.
- New `GET /rpc/messaging/stats` snapshot and read-only `aitbc messaging stats`; `aitbc-messaging` alert group (MessagingIndexLag, MessagingIndexDigestMismatch, MessagingReadErrors, MessagingVolumeSpike) with promtool tests; runbook `docs/ops/messaging-operability.md`.

