### HSTS stage 2: 1-year max-age + includeSubDomains on every response path

- The deployed hub vhost carried `Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=300"` at
  server level and inside the self-headered `/dashboard/` and `/shop/`
  locations, but nginx `add_header` is not inherited — the ~40 locations that
  define their own `add_header` (CORS and Cache-Control lines) emitted no HSTS
  at all. On 18 Oct 2026 the live vhost moved to
  `max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains` at server level and inside every
  location block that carries its own `add_header`, after the CSP rollout
  check passed. Verified live: `/`, `/explorer.html`, `/dashboard/`, `/shop/`,
  `/v1/market/status`, `/health` all return the raised header. `/health`
  additionally passes through the upstream app's own identical STS header
  (harmless per RFC 6797 — UAs process the first).
- `examples/nginx/nginx-aitbc.conf.example` now mirrors the STS lines —
  HSTS joins the mirrored server-level set for the first time (it was absent
  from the example entirely while the live vhost already carried stage 1).
- `tests/unit/test_website_api_contract.py` pins
  `Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"` in
  `EXPECTED_SERVER_HEADERS`; the self-headered-location check inherits it,
  so a config sync that drops or weakens HSTS fails loudly.

## v0.25.10

### v0.25.10 — escrow settlement passes, energy-rate guard, v11/v12 consensus pins, governance parameter tooling

**Baseline**: `v0.25.9` tagged at `217eaa9742` (2026-10-04). Sections below cover `v0.25.9..7cc552b26c` — 57 commits accrued on `main` after the tag, per the release-tag policy (`AGENTS.md`: the version's changelog is finalised in the tagged commit; later entries go to the next version's log).
**Date**: 2026-10-07.
**Tag**: `v0.25.10` (pending).


### Energy-rate guard stack (SD-7): POST band, refresher refusal, Prometheus export, shared staleness window
- `751b98935d` — `POST /v1/market/native-energy/rate` rejects implausible rates at the door (SD-7: `ait_per_eur_scaled` sat at the stub value 1 for nine days, pricing a one-hour GPU quote at 2 units instead of ~17M): a value outside the env-configured band `ENERGY_RATE_MIN/MAX_AIT_PER_EUR` (defaults **0.5–8.0 AIT/EUR**, bracketing the ~4.0 operating point with 2x headroom) is refused with 400, and an explicit int64 pre-check turns a widened-band overflow into a 400 instead of a 500 on insert (the scaled column is int64, `rate*1e18` — max must stay under ~9.22 AIT/EUR). The attestation refresher `native-energy-rate-refresh.sh` applies the same band (same env keys, same defaults) and **refuses+logs a bad stored rate instead of re-attesting it** — previously it re-posted the stored integer verbatim forever.
- `1d3c06e417` — monitoring exports the rate state as textfile Collector metrics (`aitbc_native_energy_rate_*`): stored value, freshness, last-update age, refused/missing. Alert rules flag the coordinator serving no usable rate.
- `13175eba79` — coordinator and fleet now share one freshness window (**86400 s**, env `ENERGY_RATE_STALE_AFTER_SECONDS`) instead of divergent constants.
- `b43c6d147d` — invariant test: the enforced POST band must fully cover every rate the fleet has ever run, so no in-band historical value is ever refused.
- `29445f2779` — ops runbook for the guard: env knobs, deploy, and rollback.
- `3e25a9cd5b` — deploy fix: the textfile-metrics file is written with permissions node_exporter can actually read (0600 → 0644 fix; SD-7 metrics were silently absent on fleet hosts).


### feat(chain): MSG-1 — forum messaging becomes real signed MESSAGE transactions (2026-10-15)

Forum messaging previously lived in an in-memory singleton behind
`/rpc/contracts/messaging/*` — no transaction, no persistence, no
signature, fabricated ids. MSG-1 replaces it with the on-chain design in
`docs/design/msg1-onchain-messaging.md` (director-approved with
amendments 2026-10-15).

- Wire format: `type="MESSAGE"`, `amount=0`, fee paid by the sender,
  `to` = sender, forum data namespaced at `payload.aitbc_msg`
  (`v`, `kind` post|reply, normalized `topic`, UTF-8 `body`,
  `parent` for replies, `agent_address` == recovered signer).
  `message_id` is the tx hash. No consensus change — `MESSAGE` was
  already an open zero-value type; proposer/follower/sync paths persist
  payload rows identically and reorg deletion keeps the index honest.
- Shared codec `aitbc/messaging.py` is the single source for the caps
  (`MAX_MESSAGE_BODY_BYTES = 4096` UTF-8 bytes, topic ≤ 64 normalized
  chars, 64-hex parent), normalization, envelope build/validate
  (`envelope_error`) and bridge-internal row exclusion.
- Index `aitbc_chain/messaging_index.py`: SQL cheap-filter
  (`json_extract` on SQLite) → bounded Python validity scan → keyset
  cursor. Invalid rows are dropped *before* grouping/counts/pagination
  so sealed junk cannot skew topics. No new table or migration.
- Canonical read routes `/rpc/messaging/*` (topics, messages,
  messages/{tx_hash}, search, state) — `limit` ≤ 100, opaque cursors,
  `q` ≥ 3 chars with LIKE-escaping, every response carries
  `chain_id`/`index_height`. Legacy `/rpc/contracts/messaging/*` read
  paths remain as aliases for the MCP tools.
- Admission (`_validate_transaction_admission`) and gossip
  (`gossip_transaction_drop_reason`) reject `aitbc_msg`-claiming
  payloads that fail the envelope predicate; other MESSAGE payloads are
  untouched.
- Obsolete mutation routes (`messages/post`, `topics/create`,
  `deploy/messaging`, vote, moderate, reputation) now return 501 —
  votes/moderation/reputation are MSG-2 scope.
- `AgentMessagingContract` singleton deleted; the coordinator-api SDK's
  fake local `_call_messaging_contract` now returns an honest
  not-implemented error.
- CLI `aitbc messaging send` signs the complete envelope locally
  (wallet + `--password-file`/`--password-stdin`, `--fee`, `--topic`,
  `--reply-to`, `--wait`) and submits to `/rpc/transaction`; `to`/`amount`
  are placed in the payload before signing so server-side enrichment is
  a no-op and signed bytes == verified bytes. The simulated fallback is
  gone — RPC failures exit non-zero. A public-permanence warning prints
  before every post. MCP wrappers regenerated (6 tools).
- Tests: `apps/blockchain-node/tests/test_messaging_index.py` (62)
  covers codec boundaries, round-trip sign→submit→accept,
  post-signature tamper rejection at route and consensus layer, sealed
  junk interleaved between valid rows, unresolvable parents
  (`parent_resolved: false`), bridge-row exclusion, cursor pagination;
  `tests/cli/test_commands_messaging.py` (16) covers the real-signing
  command surface.

