### 2026-09-28 — CONFIRMED: followers never verify transaction signatures (unsigned-tx hole)

The served transaction shape strips signature verification end to end:
`/rpc/blocks-range`, `/rpc/sync` export, and gossip block pushes serialize
`Transaction.model_dump()` — the signature lives only inside the nested
`envelope` column, so `_append_block` never sees a top-level `signature`
and both apply paths skip verification at every version. The nonce check
is bypassed too: `use_account_nonce_override` rewrites the recorded nonce
for unsigned txs before any comparison. Attesters sign only header fields
(`remote_attestation` signs state_root/bridge_state_root without executing
a single tx), so quorum means "a validator sent a header", not "these txs
are authorized".

A single compromised validator key can propose a block moving funds out of
any account; followers apply it. Pinned by `test_unsigned_tx_import.py`
(accepted today; flips to reject-tests at v9). Even a genuinely signed
envelope is ignored — a served row with an envelope attesting amount=10
still applies its served `value` of 999.

Live-chain audit (hub): envelope storage began at height 26722; all 240
earlier txs carry no retrievable signature — pre-v9 history can never be
signature-verified, only consistent with expected activity.

Interim mitigation applied fleet-wide (v9 fix still required):
- node2s validator key was in ~20 service env files

